$\mathrm{H}_3 \mathrm{PO}_2, \mathrm{H}_3 \mathrm{PO}_3$ and $\mathrm{H}_3 \mathrm{PO}_4$ contain one, two and three ionisable hydrogen atoms respectively.

\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{H}_3 \mathrm{PO}_2 \rightleftharpoons \mathrm{H}^{+}+\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{PO}_2^{-} \\
& \mathrm{H}_3 \mathrm{PO}_3 \rightleftharpoons \mathrm{H}^{+}+\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{PO}_3{ }^{-} \rightleftharpoons 2 \mathrm{H}^{+}+\mathrm{HPO}_3{ }^{2-} \\
& \mathrm{H}_3 \mathrm{PO}_4 \rightleftharpoons \mathrm{H}^{+}+\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{PO}_4^{-} \rightleftharpoons 2 \mathrm{H}^{+}+\mathrm{HPO}_4{ }^{2-} \\
& \rightleftharpoons 3 \mathrm{H}^{+}+\mathrm{PO}_4{ }^{3-}
\end{aligned}

